MoE LoRA training with MLX >= 0.32.1: stop gradients through the routers' expert indices.

MLX 0.32.1 (ml-explore/mlx#3820) made gradients that reach gather indices an error instead of a
silent zero, so LoRA training of these MoE models fails on its first backward step with
"[gather_axis] Cannot calculate VJP with respect to indices". MLX-LM fixed its routers the same
way (ml-explore/mlx-lm#1787, #1856; released in 0.32.0). Gradients with this line equal MLX
0.32.0's without it, bit for bit; the forward pass does not change.

Delete this patch when an MLX-VLM release carries the fix (env sync stops when the version
changes). See docs/stack.md, Known limits.

diff -ru a/mlx_vlm/models/qwen3_5_moe/language.py b/mlx_vlm/models/qwen3_5_moe/language.py
--- a/mlx_vlm/models/qwen3_5_moe/language.py
+++ b/mlx_vlm/models/qwen3_5_moe/language.py
@@ -37,6 +37,7 @@
 
         k = self.top_k
         inds = mx.argpartition(gates, kth=-k, axis=-1)[..., -k:]
+        inds = mx.stop_gradient(inds)
         scores = mx.take_along_axis(gates, inds, axis=-1)
         scores = scores / scores.sum(axis=-1, keepdims=True)
 
diff -ru a/mlx_vlm/models/qwen3_moe/language.py b/mlx_vlm/models/qwen3_moe/language.py
--- a/mlx_vlm/models/qwen3_moe/language.py
+++ b/mlx_vlm/models/qwen3_moe/language.py
@@ -99,6 +99,7 @@
 
         k = self.top_k
         inds = mx.argpartition(gates, kth=-k, axis=-1)[..., -k:]
+        inds = mx.stop_gradient(inds)
         scores = mx.take_along_axis(gates, inds, axis=-1)
         if self.norm_topk_prob:
             scores /= mx.sum(scores, axis=-1, keepdims=True)
